# Copy to .env (npm run setup does it for you). Never commit .env. npm run review and the Python tools both read it.
# Paths below are Windows examples; on macOS or Linux write /Users/you/studio-data and so on.
# Where the catalog, proxies, renders and ffmpeg live. Not the git checkout. Default: ./data beside the code.
STUDIO_DATA=D:\studio-data
# The footage folder. Read only. Google Drive for Desktop is the usual source. Default: STUDIO_DATA\footage.
STUDIO_SOURCE=D:\Footage
# Python from the studio venv. Defaults to STUDIO_DATA\venv\Scripts\python.exe (STUDIO_DATA/venv/bin/python elsewhere).
STUDIO_PY=D:\studio-data\venv\Scripts\python.exe
# ffmpeg and ffprobe. Defaults to STUDIO_DATA\bin. Needs a current build (-fps_mode).
STUDIO_TOOLS=D:\studio-data\bin
# Google Takeout zips, if you use Google Photos (point it at My Drive\Takeout). Default: STUDIO_DATA\takeout.
STUDIO_TAKEOUT=D:\Google Drive\My Drive\Takeout
# Optional API token. Set it on a shared computer: every program (and the browser, once, through the address the
# studio prints at start, /?token=...) must then carry it. The MCP server reads it from here. Empty = off.
STUDIO_API_TOKEN=
# For the MCP server and the `lazycow` npm package (npx lazycow mcp|status|api) when they run outside this folder: the
# studio folder whose .env they read. Default: the folder the double-click setup recorded. Leave empty here.
LAZYCOW_DIR=
# The Wi-Fi drop box port (Footage › Collect from others). Default 4319.
STUDIO_DROP_PORT=
# Facebook Page posting: your Meta app's ID and secret (docs/integrations.md), or enter them once in the studio.
STUDIO_FB_APP_ID=
STUDIO_FB_APP_SECRET=
# The word bank file. Default: shared/words.json in the Tsumagoi workspace, else beside the project's reels.
STUDIO_WORDS=
# Optional: a website .env to borrow an OpenRouter key from. Leave empty if you have none.
STUDIO_WEBSITE_ENV=
# Paid tagging only. The editor, the grade and the music do not need it.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Hard stop for paid calls, per local day.
STUDIO_DAILY_USD_BUDGET=2
# Set to 1 only when a person has approved a gap-fill video spend.
STUDIO_GAP_CONFIRM=0
# Extra folders of ranch footage outside STUDIO_SOURCE, semicolon-separated (they count as ranch footage).
# Google Photos picks land in STUDIO_DATA\imports and are included automatically.
STUDIO_EXTRA_SOURCES=
# Minutes between automatic checks of every footage folder for new files (0 = off).
STUDIO_WATCH_MINUTES=30
# YouTube posting: a Google Cloud "Desktop app" OAuth client (Settings › Accounts › YouTube walks you through it).
# Or leave both empty and save Google's download as STUDIO_DATA\secrets\youtube_client.json.
STUDIO_YT_CLIENT_ID=
STUDIO_YT_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Your audience's time zone (IANA name, e.g. Asia/Tokyo, Europe/London). Post times are picked and shown in it,
# so a computer abroad still schedules 19:00 where the viewers are. Empty = this computer's zone.
STUDIO_TZ=
# The Google Maps (Business Profile) listing the browser helper schedules posts on: its id from
# business.google.com/locations (docs/helper.md). Empty = the helper finds it when there is only one listing.
STUDIO_GBP_LOCATION=
# Which browser the helper drives (docs/helper.md): empty = your own Chrome through the Playwright extension when it is
# installed, else its own window; "extension" or "own" to choose.
STUDIO_HELPER_BROWSER=
# Skips the one "Allow & select" click: paste the line the Playwright extension's connect page copies. It is a key to
# your browser; keep it only in .env.
PLAYWRIGHT_MCP_EXTENSION_TOKEN=
# Whose studio this is, shown beside the logo (e.g. your shop or channel name). Empty hides it.
STUDIO_WORKSPACE=
# Projects: the list of projects (one per brand or client) lives here, outside every project. Default ~/.lazycow.
# Make and switch projects in the studio (the name chip beside the logo); each gets STUDIO_HOME/projects/<id>.
STUDIO_HOME=
# Run a second studio beside the first. Google sign-in returns to the studio's own port (a Desktop-type Google app accepts
# any port on 127.0.0.1), so YouTube can be connected from either.
STUDIO_PORT=
# 1: a studio for looking only (tests, a second copy on the same data): nothing posts, books, swaps, checks or
# renders by itself, and the Chrome helper does not start. What a person presses still works.
STUDIO_QUIET=
# A second studio pinned to one project (with STUDIO_PORT and usually STUDIO_QUIET=1): it opens that project whatever the
# main studio has open, and never switches. e.g. STUDIO_PROJECT=highlands-coast STUDIO_PORT=4318 STUDIO_QUIET=1 npm run review
STUDIO_PROJECT=
# Where a project keeps drafts per network, approved files, and reel project files (set per project automatically).
STUDIO_DRAFTS=
STUDIO_READY=
STUDIO_PROJECTS=
# Leave empty. The original Tsumagoi Work&Camp workspace (the "ranch overlay": shared/reels.json and its files, not in
# a public clone) switches on by itself where its files are. 0 forces it off, 1 on, for the main project only.
STUDIO_RANCH=
# AI assist (Settings › AI saves these; docs/ai-api.md). Every paid call is priced first and refused over a limit.
# fal.ai: slow motion, sharpen, music for a reel, Japanese voice, living photo.
FAL_KEY=
# OpenRouter key for the AI reviewer only. Kept under this name so paid tagging (OPENROUTER_API_KEY above) stays off.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY_PARKED=
# Turn paid tagging on with the reviewer's key (off unless set to on).
STUDIO_PAID_TAGGING=
# Together AI (checked and saved; living photos use fal, which is cheaper).
TOGETHER_API_KEY=
# AI limits in US dollars: per reel, and for all AI spend together. The daily budget above also applies.
STUDIO_AI_REEL_CAP_USD=2
STUDIO_AI_TOTAL_CAP_USD=20
# Optional: the reviewer's OpenRouter model (must accept video). Default google/gemini-3.8-flash.
STUDIO_AI_REVIEW_MODEL=

# The YouTube channel this project posts to (an @handle or a UC... id). Uploads to any other channel are refused.
STUDIO_YT_CHANNEL=

# Draft reels made by themselves from new footage (watcher or Google Photos import), per day. 0 turns it off.
STUDIO_AUTO_DRAFTS=2

# The Google account whose Photos the studio imports from (the sign-in opens on it and refuses another).
STUDIO_GPHOTOS_ACCOUNT=

# The LinkedIn company page reels are scheduled on (the number in linkedin.com/company/<number>/admin).
STUDIO_LINKEDIN_PAGE=

# Firecrawl key for the Ideas page (Settings › Keys & AI saves it here; docs/research-api.md).
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=
# Live Firecrawl requests per day for Ideas (cached results stay free). Default 60.
STUDIO_RESEARCH_DAILY_CAP=
# 1 = new reels follow what Results learned without asking each time (docs/perf-api.md). Off unless set.
STUDIO_PERF_STEER=

